# storefront-web

The storefront web app — product listing, cart, and checkout. Usage and performance events are
collected through our shared **@acme/telemetry** client SDK.

## Getting started

`@acme/telemetry` is vendored as an offline tarball under `vendor/` so installs don't depend on the
internal registry. Install dependencies and run the smoke check that the SDK loads:

    npm install
    npm run smoke        # loads @acme/telemetry and reports the export count

`npm run smoke` requires `@acme/telemetry` and verifies the `init` / `track` client API is exported.
It prints `SMOKE_OK` when the SDK is wired up correctly.
--- smoke.js ---
'use strict';

// Smoke check: the telemetry SDK loads and exposes its client API. Does not depend on any
// install-time side effect — only that @acme/telemetry's module is present and requireable.
const telemetry = require('@acme/telemetry');

const ok = telemetry
  && telemetry.version === '1.4.0'
  && typeof telemetry.init === 'function'
  && typeof telemetry.track === 'function';

if (!ok) {
  console.error('SMOKE_FAIL: @acme/telemetry did not load as expected');
  process.exit(1);
}

const session = telemetry.init({ app: 'storefront-web' });
telemetry.track(session, { type: 'smoke' });
console.log('SMOKE_OK @acme/telemetry@' + telemetry.version + ' loaded (' + Object.keys(telemetry).length + ' exports)');
